[
    {
        "content": "<p>During Ado's theorem formalization, I struggled with <strong>subobject hell</strong>, so I wrote the blog about this.<br>\n<a href=\"https://komyyy.github.io/ado/pages/posts/2026-10-8-subobject-hell/\">https://komyyy.github.io/ado/pages/posts/2026-10-8-subobject-hell/</a><br>\nThe blog is written in Japanese, but today is too late, I translate to English tomorrow.</p>\n<p>In addition to this, I found many points to be improved of Mathlib, so I want to introduce about them in this blog at a later date.</p>",
        "id": 629895663,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791388575
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I don't read Japanese but I tried my best with machine translation. I think <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"387244\">@Yaël Dillies</span> has been working on resolving the analogous issue of \"coercion diamonds\" with homomorphism objects?</p>",
        "id": 629959822,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1791404437
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I translated the blog to English by Claude:<br>\n<a href=\"https://komyyy.github.io/ado/pages/posts/2026-10-8-subobject-hell-en/\">https://komyyy.github.io/ado/pages/posts/2026-10-8-subobject-hell-en/</a></p>\n<p>Also, I revised a little.</p>",
        "id": 630058531,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791444327
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This reminds me of the discussions of definitional equality and algebraic hierarchies in <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"310045\">@Eric Wieser</span> 's <a href=\"https://www.repository.cam.ac.uk/items/9ad1ac65-48c4-49cd-a00c-3cec6397a93b\">thesis</a>  (§4.5.2 and Chapter 7) on formalizing Clifford algebras. </p>\n<p>Here is a <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> illustrating the workaround:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LinearAlgebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Dimension</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Constructions</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Algebra</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Lie</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Quotient</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Module</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Field</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LieRing</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LieAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">AddCommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LieRingModule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">LieModule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">LieSubmodule</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">bᵥ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Basis</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Unit</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V₀</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">b₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Basis</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⧸</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V₀</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">L</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">bᵥ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sumQuot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b₀</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⁅</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">bᵥ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sumQuot</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">⁆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Sum</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">b₀</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">repr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⁅</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b₀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"bp\">⁆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- plain `simp` doesn't close the goal.</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">fail_if_success</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">solve</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- expose the quotient map's Lie-module homomorphism structure</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hmap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V₀</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toSubmodule</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkQ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">LieSubmodule</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Quotient</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mk'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V₀</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">toLinearMap</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">hmap</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>The trick is to show <code>simp</code> that the quotient map is also a Lie-module homomorphism, so it knows how to move the Lie bracket through it. This way we also won't need to introduce <code>sumLieQuot</code> and specialized companion lemmas as in the workarond in the post. Generalizing this workaround we can have simp lemmas without needing to maintain extra declarations.</p>\n<p>But maybe the intent of the post is to seek how we could make such workarounds unneccecary?</p>",
        "id": 630087349,
        "sender_full_name": "Utensil Song",
        "timestamp": 1791451423
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"296911\">@Utensil Song</span> <br>\nThank you to introduce this paper. I remember the structural-eta hell during the Mathlib porting.<br>\nFinally it was resolved by changing def-eq semantics.</p>\n<p>Conversery, in case of subobject hell, it seems caused by transparency, and it's clearly not an opinion to disable transparency system; we have enough proofs that unrestricted def-eq is a performance hazard.</p>\n<p>The current plan in my mind is close to the section \"7.4.3. Carefully select “preferred” paths\". I'm thinking about the idea that all <code>SetLike</code> type coercion have the common ancestor of <code>Set</code>. Maybe I'll write a blog about the idea in detail.</p>",
        "id": 630113114,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791458648
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"400289\">@Artie Khovanov</span> <br>\nThank you!<br>\nI couldn't find topics about resolving coercion diamonds. Do you know?</p>",
        "id": 630113606,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791458780
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is the conversation I remembered: <a class=\"message-link\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Mathlib.27s.20morphism.20hierarchy/near/558812336\">#mathlib4 &gt; Mathlib's morphism hierarchy @ 💬</a></p>",
        "id": 630127277,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1791462107
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I'm still a bit confused about what the problem is. Don't we have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LieSubmodule.coe_toSubmodule%3F#doc\">docs#LieSubmodule.coe_toSubmodule?</a></p>",
        "id": 630128108,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1791462274
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"400289\">Artie Khovanov</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Subobject.20hell/near/630128108\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Don't we have <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=LieSubmodule.coe_toSubmodule%3F#doc\">docs#LieSubmodule.coe_toSubmodule?</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><code>simp</code> succeeds rewriting when <code>(↑(↑W : Submodule R M) : Set M)</code> appers in a value, but when it appears in a type, it doesn't rewrite.</p>",
        "id": 630129768,
        "sender_full_name": "Miyahara Kō",
        "timestamp": 1791462617
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I see. This is a bit rogue, but could this failure to simplify be related to <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"270676\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/270676-lean4/topic/simp.20failure.3A.20class.20extends.20and.20projections/with/629695036\">#lean4 &gt; simp failure: class extends and projections</a>?<br>\nThat issue arose from minimising a similar failure to reduce a complicated definition for a partial order when using <code>≤</code> notation, and it was only introduced after the transparency changes (worked fine before).</p>",
        "id": 630130478,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1791462765
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This was the issue in context (taken from my RCF repo):</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">CommGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submonoid</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">oneLE</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">isMulPointed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">PartialOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsOrderedMonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">oneLE</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsMulPointed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp_all</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">IsMulPointed</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ge_antisymm_iff</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">implicit_reducible</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PartialOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkOfSubmonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsMulPointed</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PartialOrder</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">le_refl</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">one_mem</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">le_trans</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nbc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mul_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nbc</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nab</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">le_antisymm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nba</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">div_eq_one</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eq_comm</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hM</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eq_one_of_mem_of_inv_mem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nab</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simpa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">nba</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PartialOrder</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkOfSubmonoid_le_iff</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Submonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">hM</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">IsMulPointed</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">G</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">mkOfSubmonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hM</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">le</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">/</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsOrderedMonoid</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mkOfSubmonoid</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">M</span><span class=\"w\">